      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "NlmCategory": "OBJECTIVE",
          "Label": "AIM",
          "content": "To investigate the effect of high mobility group protein box-1 (HMGB1) siRNA on proliferation and apoptosis of retinoblastoma (Rb) cells."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "METHODS",
          "content": "The expression of HMGB1 in Rb cells were detected by real-time polymerase chain reaction (RT-PCR) and Western blot. Chemically synthesized HMGB1 siRNA was transfected into Y79 cells. The inhibitory rate was also examined by RT-PCR and Western blot. After HMGB1 siRNA transfection, the cell proliferation was analyzed by MTT, and cell apoptosis was detected by Caspase-3 active detection kit. Cell cycle distribution and apoptosis were detected by flow cytometry."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "RESULTS",
          "Label": "RESULTS",
          "content": "The expression of HMGB1 significantly elevated in Rb cells (P<0.01). After transfected by siRNA, the HMGB1 protein level of Y79 cells was significantly reduced (P<0.01). After siRNA interference HMGB1, the proportion of proliferating cells reduced, and the proportion of quiescent cells increased (P<0.05). In addition, apoptosis rate of Y79 cells increased from 2.03% to 9.10% after interfering with HMGB1 siRNA (P<0.05)."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "CONCLUSION",
          "content": "Specific HMGB1 siRNA can inhibit the expression of HMGB1. The effect may be attributed to inhibit the proliferation and promote cell apoptosis."
        }
      ]},
